subject: fix(messages): audit-found bugs — BoardView reconciliation, fetch race, curl export, TimelineView

Fixes from the code-audit subagent (verified in main session):

1. BoardView (B1/B2/B3): replaced setState-during-render seeding with a
   moves-map + derived-columns pattern. User drags are the only state;
   everything else derives from the current filtered `grouped` data — new
   fingerprints appear, stale ones disappear, no render-time setState, and
   `move` uses a functional update (no stale closure). Also added
   onDragOver/onDrop to the column container so drops onto empty columns
   work (U3).

2. conversation.tokens null-safety (D1): ConversationView + TraceTreeView
   now use `tokens?.prompt ?? 0` — no crash if tokens missing.

3. Fetch race (R1): page load() now aborts the previous in-flight request
   via AbortController, so a slow response for an old filter can't
   overwrite newer results; aborts are swallowed, loading only clears when
   the latest request settles.

4. curl export (A3): buildCurl (page + export route) now emits a usable
   placeholder endpoint instead of empty URL, and detects `_truncated`
   payloads with a note + preview instead of dumping the marker.

5. TimelineView (U1/U2): body segment renders only when real body latency
   exists (total > ttft); ttft fallback no longer mislabels ttft as total.

VERIFICATION: build passes, deployed to 20131, Board view browser-verified
(5 fingerprint cards in New, drop placeholders in empty columns).

Part of: Messages Page + Error Inbox plan (P1 hardening)

